# Plan → Grill gate

When designing a plan (Plan mode or an explicit planning request):

## Offer grilling when ANY of these hold

- Multiple modules / libraries / workflows change
- Irreversible choice (public API, data format, agent policy, release channel)
- New abstraction or process that will outlive this chat
- User is unsure between two+ approaches

Then: say you recommend `/grill-me` (or the `grilling` skill), ask one clarifying question if needed, and wait. Do not implement until they confirm the plan or decline grilling.

## Skip grilling when

- Single-file / obvious bugfix
- CI green-up, typo, or mechanical retarget
- User already gave a locked decision and said to execute

Do **not** auto-start a full grill on every plan — offer it, then proceed only after confirmation or an explicit “skip grill / just plan”.
